            "function": {
              "name": "extracted_data",
              "arguments": "{\"overview\":\"The SalesTech CRM project is red because vendor and customer dependencies threaten ecommerce timing, while a separate policy-track issue is resolved.\",\"summaries\":[{\"iteration\":1,\"missingFacts\":[],\"expandedSummary\":\"Acme Insurance’s SalesTech CRM project is RED due to Alfatech’s delayed document production system, which is expected to delay the ecommerce track by two sprints. SysCorp is adding resources to recover time once the system is available.\"},{\"iteration\":2,\"missingFacts\":[\"Acme has not provided ecommerce test data, putting stabilization at risk unless resolved by month-end.\",\"Steerco insists on the existing release schedule despite the risks, and Acme executives want SalesTech to validate SysCorp’s assessment.\",\"SysCorp missed two recent calls and has not responded to an escalation to its leadership.\"],\"expandedSummary\":\"Acme Insurance’s SalesTech CRM project is RED because Alfatech’s delayed document production system is expected to push the ecommerce track by two sprints; SysCorp plans to add resources after delivery to mitigate the delay. Separately, missing customer test data could affect stabilization unless supplied by month-end, while Steerco maintains the release schedule despite the risks. Acme executives are seeking SalesTech’s confirmation of SysCorp’s assessment, but SysCorp’s two missed calls and unanswered leadership escalation have left SalesTech without adequate insight.\"},{\"iteration\":3,\"missingFacts\":[\"The customer is discussing resolution of the vendor delay with Alfatech.\",\"The Integration Proxy connectivity issue blocking the policy track was resolved on August 30, 2021, and that track is now GREEN.\",\"The production deployment plan was finalized August 15 and is awaiting customer approval.\",\"Steerco was informed of the potential impact the prior week.\"],\"expandedSummary\":\"As of September 1, 2021, Acme Insurance’s SalesTech CRM project is RED because Alfatech’s delayed document production system is expected to delay ecommerce by two sprints; Acme is discussing resolution with the vendor, and SysCorp plans to deploy extra resources once the system is ready. Missing customer test data threatens the stabilization schedule unless resolved by month-end, and Steerco—briefed the previous week—still insists on the release schedule because its marketing campaign is underway. Acme executives want SalesTech to validate SysCorp’s assessment, but SysCorp missed two recent calls and has not responded to a leadership escalation. The Integration Proxy issue blocking the policy track was resolved August 30, making that track GREEN; the production deployment plan was finalized August 15 and remains pending customer approval.\"}]}"
            }
